message: "Please cite this software when using the formal proofs or exact computational checks."
type: software
title: "BTP/PBF: formal proofs and exact computational checks"
authors:
  - family-names: "Mañas"
    given-names: "Manuel"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3764-5737"
date-released: "2026-10-19"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ManuelManas/btp-pbf-verification"
url: "https://github.com/ManuelManas/btp-pbf-verification/releases/tag/2026-10-19-stability"
abstract: >-
  Lean proofs and manuscript-to-formalization correspondence for banded total
  positivity and positive bidiagonal factorizations. Includes inverse-minor
  existence criteria, Toeplitz factorization, the complete weighted-shift
  stability lemma, a periodic scalar criterion, and the abstract quantitative
  perturbation-radius argument. Explicit hypotheses and partial coverage are
  distinguished from the unformalized general analytic and spectral results.
  Historical exact and high-precision computational checks are preserved.
